			"notes": "# Emotify 0.8.1\n\nThis release adds a smooth hotbar emoji feedback indicator, an in-game client settings toggle, and expanded settings layout support across all supported loaders and platforms.\n\n### Highlights\n\n* **Hotbar Emoji Indicator:** Displays a subtle 16×16 px preview icon directly above the hotbar when sending an emoji, synchronized with your overhead emotion lifecycle.\n* **Smooth Motion & Zero Stutter:** Rendered with floating-point GPU interpolation for smooth ease-out entry, sustain, and smoothstep fade-out exit across all GUI scales.\n* **Client Settings Toggle:** Added an in-game toggle button in the mod settings screen to enable or disable the hotbar indicator at any time.\n* **Expanded Settings Panel:** Symmetrically expanded panel geometry to 6 rows while retaining consistent button heights and padding.\n* **Multi-loader Persistence:** Full configuration persistence across Fabric (`emotify-client.properties`) and NeoForge (`emotify-client.toml`).\n* **Localization:** Complete English and Russian translations for all new UI components and tooltips.\n\n### Requirements & Compatibility\n\n* **Fabric:** Minecraft 1.21.1, 1.21.8, 1.21.11, and 26.2 (requires Fabric API & Fabric Language Kotlin)\n* **NeoForge:** Minecraft 1.21.1, 1.21.8, 1.21.11, and 26.2 (requires Kotlin for Forge)\n* **Paper / Purpur / Folia:** Minecraft 1.21.1, 1.21.8, 1.21.11, and 26.2 (no extra dependencies)\n* **Java:** Java 21 on 1.21.x; Java 25 on 26.2\n\n### Artifacts\n\n| Platform | Minecraft Version | Artifact |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Fabric | 1.21.1 | `emotify-fabric-1.21.1-0.8.1.jar` |\n| Fabric | 1.21.8 | `emotify-fabric-1.21.8-0.8.1.jar` |\n| Fabric | 1.21.11 | `emotify-fabric-1.21.11-0.8.1.jar` |\n| Fabric | 26.2 | `emotify-fabric-26.2-0.8.1.jar` |\n| NeoForge | 1.21.1 | `emotify-neoforge-1.21.1-0.8.1.jar` |\n| NeoForge | 1.21.8 | `emotify-neoforge-1.21.8-0.8.1.jar` |\n| NeoForge | 1.21.11 | `emotify-neoforge-1.21.11-0.8.1.jar` |\n| NeoForge | 26.2 | `emotify-neoforge-26.2-0.8.1.jar` |\n| Paper / Purpur / Folia | 1.21.1 – 26.2 | `emotify-paper-1.21-0.8.1.jar` |\n\nPlayers who want to send and see emotions must install the Emotify client matching their loader and Minecraft version. Other players can join normally."
