			"notes": "# Emotify 0.8.0\n\nThis release adds official support for Minecraft 26.2, native Folia multi-threading support, critical rendering and depth occlusion fixes, and GUI stability improvements across all platforms.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- **Minecraft 26.2 Platform Support:** Added official Fabric, NeoForge, and Paper/Purpur/Folia support with Java 25 compatibility.\n- **Native Folia Support:** Fully regionized scheduling, thread-safe asynchronous packet routing, and dynamic world lifecycle handling on Folia servers.\n- **Render Layer & Depth Fixes:** Fixed emojis becoming transparent against water, nether portals, clouds, sky, and separate composited layers.\n- **Occlusion Stability:** Fixed billboard fade-in and fade-out rendering to strictly prevent emojis from showing through solid blocks.\n- **GUI & Search Box Fixes:** Resolved 1.21.1 client picker initialization crashes and removed unwanted text shadows in the search box.\n- **Cross-Platform Compatibility:** Full protocol parity across all supported Fabric/NeoForge clients (1.21.1, 1.21.8, 1.21.11, 26.2) and Paper/Purpur/Folia servers.\n\n### Requirements\n\n#### Fabric\n- Minecraft 1.21.1, 1.21.8, 1.21.11, or 26.2\n- Fabric Loader 0.19.3 or newer\n- Fabric API (matching Minecraft version)\n- Fabric Language Kotlin 1.13.12+kotlin.2.4.0 or newer\n- Java 21 (1.21.1–1.21.11) / Java 25 (26.2)\n\n#### NeoForge\n- Minecraft 1.21.1, 1.21.8, 1.21.11, or 26.2\n- NeoForge:\n  - 1.21.1: `21.1.234+`\n  - 1.21.8: `21.8.54+`\n  - 1.21.11: `21.11.45+`\n  - 26.2: `26.2.0.59+`\n- Kotlin for Forge:\n  - `5.12.0+` on 1.21.1 and 1.21.8\n  - `6.3.0+` on 1.21.11 and 26.2\n- Java 21 (1.21.1–1.21.11) / Java 25 (26.2)\n\n#### Paper / Purpur / Folia\n- Minecraft 1.21.1, 1.21.8, 1.21.11, or 26.2\n- Paper, Purpur, or Folia server\n- Java 21 (1.21.1–1.21.11) / Java 25 (26.2)\n- No additional server dependencies required\n\nPlayers without Emotify can still join supported servers, but they cannot send or see emotions."
		},
