			"notes": "# Emotify 0.6.1\n\nThis patch improves multi-emoji animation endings, custom emoji reliability, rendering cleanup, and server lifecycle handling.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- Reworked Ribbon Weave, Lantern Release, and Echo Bloom endings.\n- Added synchronized group movement with smooth acceleration, curved upward flight, and shared squash-and-stretch.\n- Preserved staggered disappearance without allowing lower emojis to catch up with the others.\n- Fixed custom emoji upload state after an interrupted selection request.\n- Fixed stale render resources after removing local custom emojis.\n- Fixed Paper dimension identity data remaining retained after dynamic world unloads.\n- Strengthened NeoForge release metadata validation.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Fabric\n\n- Minecraft 1.21.1\n- Fabric Loader 0.19.3 or newer\n- Fabric API\n- Fabric Language Kotlin\n- Java 21\n\n### NeoForge\n\n- Minecraft 1.21.1\n- NeoForge 21.1.234 or newer\n- Kotlin for Forge 5.12.0 or a newer compatible 5.x release\n- Java 21\n\n### Paper / Purpur\n\n- Minecraft 1.21.1\n- Paper or Purpur 1.21.1\n- Java 21\n\nPlayers without Emotify can still join supported servers, but they cannot send or see emotions."
		},
