			"notes": "# Emotify 0.6.0\n\nEmotify 0.6.0 is the stable feature-complete release for Minecraft 1.21.1. It adds a fourth animation style, improves custom emoji feedback, fixes cross-loader GIF sharing, and completes a broad reliability and performance pass across all supported platforms.\n\n## Highlights\n\n### Animations\n\n- Added the new Echo Bloom animation.\n- Emotify now includes four distinct animation styles.\n- Refined entrances, living motion, staggered exits, vertical flight, and fade timing.\n- Improved Lantern Release so both elements disappear naturally while moving upward.\n- Removed unwanted horizontal movement during Echo Bloom exits.\n\n### Custom emoji experience\n\n- Added a compact one-time Shift + right-click saving hint.\n- Invalid PNG, JPEG, and GIF files now remain visible as passive darkened cards.\n- Detailed localized loading errors are shown when hovering an invalid file.\n- Working custom emojis always remain above invalid files.\n- Fixed black or corrupted frames in some shared GIF files, including certain Aseprite exports.\n- Improved incremental scanning and reuse of unchanged decoded assets and textures.\n\n### Reliability and performance\n\n- Added client configuration schema 2 with safe migration.\n- Moved expensive custom asset decoding and verification away from critical client and server threads.\n- Added bounded queues, exact memory accounting, stale-result protection, permission rechecks, and safer shutdown handling.\n- Reduced repeated custom asset encoding and transfer work through bounded caching.\n- Improved malformed payload rejection, traffic accounting, lifecycle cleanup, and reconnect handling.\n\n## Available builds\n\n- NeoForge client and server\n- Fabric client and server\n- Paper and Purpur server plugin\n\nAll builds target Minecraft 1.21.1 and Java 21.\n\nPlayers without Emotify can still join supported servers, but they cannot send or see emotions."
		},
