			"notes": "## Emotify 0.5.2\n\nThis maintenance release fixes custom-emoji quick-slot persistence and strengthens custom asset and configuration handling across NeoForge, Fabric, Paper, and Purpur.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Fixed custom emojis disappearing from NeoForge quick slots after restarting the game.\n- Verified equivalent custom quick-slot persistence on Fabric.\n- Kept built-in and custom quick slots independent from favorites.\n- Added automatic cleanup when an assigned local custom-emoji file has been removed.\n- Prevented incomplete scans, decoding failures, capacity limits, or directory limits from accidentally deleting assignments.\n- Updated the open picker immediately after custom-library reconciliation.\n- Avoided redundant asynchronous configuration writes when no state changed.\n- Improved descriptor-safe handling of long Unicode custom-emoji filenames.\n- Hardened NeoForge, Fabric, and Paper configuration reads against non-regular paths.\n- Revalidated bounded packet decoding, upload leases, traffic budgets, rate limits, audience limits, and weighted custom-asset caches.\n- Kept Protocol 1.6 unchanged.\n\n### Downloads\n\n- `emotify-neoforge-1.21.1-0.5.2.jar`\n- `emotify-fabric-1.21.1-0.5.2.jar`\n- `emotify-paper-1.21-0.5.2.jar`\n\n### Requirements\n\n- Minecraft 1.21.1\n- Java 21\n- NeoForge 21.1.234 or newer with Kotlin for Forge 5.12.0 or a compatible 5.x release\n- Fabric Loader 0.19.3 or newer with Fabric API and Fabric Language Kotlin\n- Paper or Purpur 1.21.1 for the server plugin\n\nNo protocol migration or configuration reset is required for this release."
		}
